WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.470
A lettuce plant.

2
00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:02.590
No field.

3
00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:03.790
No soil.

4
00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:06.050
Its roots grow in water.

5
00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:10.810
Out in the world, there are
more than 570 million farms.

6
00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.350
Most are small and family-run.

7
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:19.390
Small farms, under 2 hectares, work only
about 12 per cent of the world's farmland.

8
00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.890
So is a lettuce with
no soil still farming?

9
00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:24.670
Does farming need a field?

10
00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.090
Or a farmer who sells the crop?

11
00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.950
In this mission, you'll sort
farms by what they grow,

12
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.510
and by who eats the food.

13
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:35.270
Then you'll take a farm
apart, step by step,

14
00:00:35.320 --> 00:00:37.030
and see how it works.

15
00:00:37.080 --> 00:00:42.030
Your mission: decide whether a farm
with no soil still counts as farming.
